// ## 6. Pass-4 — Drift (self-claims vs ground truth)

// Ground truth: `git describe --tags --abbrev=0` = `v0.6.28`.

// | Source | Line | Claim | Drift |
// |--------|-----:|-------|-------|
// | `server/lsp_version.oo` | 10 | `return "0.6.21";` | **+0.0.7 (function returns wrong version)** |
// | `qa/probe_double_run.oo` | 8 (comment) | "lsp_facade_version is 0.6.21 and deterministic" | **+0.0.7** |
// | `qa/probe_double_run.oo` | 29 (assertion) | `if v1 == "0.6.21" { pass("version SSoT 0.6.21") }` | **+0.0.7 (self-fulfilling)** |
// | `qa/probe_execute_command.oo` | 8 (comment) | "ooda.lsp.version returns 0.6.21" | **+0.0.7** |
// | `qa/probe_execute_command.oo` | 23 (assertion) | `if str_index_of(v, "0.6.21") < 0 { fail("version: " + v) }` | **+0.0.7 (self-fulfilling)** |
// | `qa/probe_initialize.oo` | 10 (comment) | "lsp_facade_version equals 0.6.21" | **+0.0.7** |
// | `qa/probe_initialize.oo` | 35 (assertion) | `if ver != "0.6.21" { fail("version drift: " + ver) }` | **+0.0.7 (self-fulfilling)** |
// | `qa/probe_session.oo` | 30 (assertion) | `if str_index_of(lsp_facade_version(), "0.6.21") < 0 { fail("version") }` | **+0.0.7 (self-fulfilling)** |
// | `cli/cmd_lsp.oo` | 75 (runtime) | `println("lsp v" + lsp_facade_version());` | **+0.0.7 (CLI prints wrong version to users)** |
// | `methods/lsp_execute_command.oo` | 20 (runtime) | `lsp_facade_version()` in JSON-RPC response | **+0.0.7 (JSON-RPC returns wrong version to clients)** |
// | `openOODA/docs/INDEX.oot` | 39 | `lsp v0.6.28` | match ✓ |
// | `org audit 2026-09-10` | line 155 | `lsp v0.6.28` | match ✓ |
// | `moonshot_scorecard.oot` | — | (no direct lsp claim) | N/A |
// | `lsp/ANCHOR.oo` | 5 (meta-ref) | "Engine version is lsp_facade_version() in server/lsp_version.oo" | OK (meta-reference, no version pin) |
// | `lsp/AGENT.md` | 27-29 (§3) | "Engine version is `lsp_facade_version()` in `server/lsp_version.oo`" | OK (meta-reference, no version pin) |
// | `lsp/.github/workflows/ci.yml` | 172-174 | downloads `v0.0.10` for **blackbox** (cross-repo dep) | match (other repo's SSoT) |

// ## 7. Pass-5 — Validator (static analysis of test-vs-function closed loops)

// The lsp audit has no MCP tools (the `mcp__blackbox__*` family is
// blackbox-specific). The host-compiled execution path is broken
// per org audit 2026-09-10 NOTE n1 (oodac build fails at `print`).
// So the validator pass is **static analysis**, not end-to-end
// execution.

// | Sub-check | Result | Evidence |
// |-----------|--------|----------|
// | Function-vs-test closed loop detection | **FAIL (4 probes)** | probe_double_run.oo:29, probe_execute_command.oo:23, probe_initialize.oo:35, probe_session.oo:30 all call `lsp_facade_version()` (or a handler that calls it) and assert the result equals the literal `"0.6.21"`. The test passes only if the function returns the value the test checks. There is no external ground truth in the test. |
// | Runtime reporting points | **DRIFT** | `cli/cmd_lsp.oo:75` prints the version to stdout when users run the CLI. `methods/lsp_execute_command.oo:20` returns the version as a JSON-RPC response when an LSP client calls `ooda.lsp.version`. Both report `0.6.21` to users, not `0.6.28`. |
// | ANCHOR.oo claim verification | PASS | `ANCHOR.oo:5` says "Engine version is lsp_facade_version() in server/lsp_version.oo". The file `VERSION` does not exist. The function `lsp_facade_version` exists at the named path. The claim is structurally true; the value it returns is wrong (see Drift). |

// **Pathology:** 4 qa/ tests are self-fulfilling closed loops. They
// "verify" the version by calling the version function and checking
// the function's own return value. If you fix the function to return
// the correct version (`0.6.28`), all 4 tests will FAIL until you
// also bump the 4 assertion literals. The "tests are green" signal
// in this repo's CI is misleading — it's a single-function closed
// loop, not a real verification. This is documented as M2 below.

// ## 8. Findings by severity

// **CRITICAL (0):** none. The INDEX.oot:39 line `lsp v0.6.28` is
// independently verified by `git describe`; the drift is process
// drift, not a release-blocker.

// **MAJOR (2):**

//   M1. **7-source version stamp drift.** `server/lsp_version.oo:10`
//       (the function itself), 4 qa/ probes (`probe_double_run.oo:8,29`;
//       `probe_execute_command.oo:8,23`; `probe_initialize.oo:10,35`;
//       `probe_session.oo:30`), and 2 runtime reporting points
//       (`cli/cmd_lsp.oo:75`; `methods/lsp_execute_command.oo:20`) all
//       claim version `0.6.21`. The ground-truth tag is `v0.6.28`.
//       Drift is +0.0.7. The runtime reporting points are user-visible:
//       the CLI prints the wrong version to stdout, and the JSON-RPC
//       `ooda.lsp.version` handler returns the wrong version to LSP
//       clients. (Per plan Q1: kept at MAJOR; the moonshot-equivalent
//       line in `INDEX.oot:39` is independently verified, so this is
//       documentation/process drift, not a release-blocker. Upgrade
//       to CRITICAL only if a real downstream consumer reports a
//       version-mismatch incident.) Owner: orchestrator lane. RULES
//       §1.4 (Honesty), §1.21 (Versioning), §1.24 (Auto-release).

//   M2. **4 qa/ probe drivers are self-fulfilling closed loops.** Per
//       Pass 5: probe_double_run, probe_execute_command,
//       probe_initialize, and probe_session all call
//       `lsp_facade_version()` and assert the result equals the
//       literal `"0.6.21"`. The tests pass only if the function
//       returns the value the test checks. There is no external
//       source of truth. The "tests are green" signal is misleading:
//       if the maintainer bumps the function to `0.6.28` without
//       also bumping the 4 assertion literals, all 4 tests will
//       FAIL — but for the wrong reason (the test is checking the
//       wrong value). This is process-integrity damage, not a code
//       defect. RULES §1.4 (Honesty), §1.7 (Verified on-disk
//       features), §1.10 (Double-run invariant).

// **MINOR (1):**

//   m1. `wire/lsp_jsonrpc.oo` is at 255/256 (1 line of headroom).
//       Any future addition pushes it over the §1.8 cap and forces
//       a split. RULES §1.8.

// **NOTE (3):**

//   n1. `ANCHOR.oo:5` and `AGENT.md:27-29` are honest meta-references:
//       they say "Engine version is `lsp_facade_version()`" without
//       pinning a version number. This is the correct pattern. The
//       drift is in the function body, not in the meta-references.
//       (Documented for transparency.)
//   n2. The moonshot scorecard (`openOODA/openOODA/scripts/moonshot_scorecard.oot`)
//       contains 0 references to `lsp`. The lsp is high-leverage for
//       every IDE-integration user but is not one of the 8 moonshot
//       lines. (Documented; not a finding.)
//   n3. The 4 governance locks (re-derived against lsp/ alone) all
//       PASS. The lock pipeline is not the source of the drift; the
//       drift is in the version function and its test assertions.

